coi ro do la lojban. banli

In jboselkei I ran into this usage of {pensi'u} in the sense of meet
[each other]:

mi'o pensi'u

...which was intended to mean "I and you meet each other"

pensi'u = penmi + simxu = meeting-type of mutual.
simxu means "x1 (set) has members who mutually/reciprocally x2"

My question is, can {mi'o} be used in a place of set?
What is it indentical to, {mi .e do}, {mi joi do} or {mi ce do}?


